  "body": "## What changed\n\nFit arcs over eligible closed model-source 2D Chamfer passes with the existing sided fitter. Cap the fit by the operation tolerance and the usual arc-fit limit. The simulator and post receive the same fitted moves. The open-model-edge path keeps its existing generation. Saved 2D Chamfer caches are stale once so that they regenerate against these inputs.\n\nNOW step 1. The fork default branch is synced at v0.27.0. This upstream branch starts at c79c9b24fc0a00386ba1c74b8a0a900ff7e89193.\n\n## Validation\n\n- On the unchanged upstream base, `closed_model_chamfer_preserves_circular_interpolation` failed because the sampled circle stayed linear. It passes on the candidate for both sides and directions, with zero and positive cone setback. `chamfer_circular` passed 11/11, including existing open and straight controls.\n- The independent synthetic app fixture `closed_model_chamfer_posts_haas_arcs_through_the_stock_gate` passed through the normal gate and posted three arc blocks in 24 program lines. `chamfer_modelled_edge` passed 8/8.\n- Selected quick gate on head 29690de93619e1da7271eac60e414b9c9e9a4561 passed 11/11 steps, 482 tests, zero failed and four ignored. The catalog suites passed 44+1+1, with four release-only cases ignored in the main catalog. `first_part_programs` passed 2/2 and `solid_law_goldens` 7/7.\n- The trial merge against upstream e4b08e95b9860a6257a10e3f7e7c14f0b71cc1c2 was clean. Whitespace checks passed.\n- Light lane remains unrun. The local build filesystem switched to read-only after the quick checks. Controller timing is outside the synthetic test coverage.\n\nWriter record: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/4411#issuecomment-7225543038\n\nEffort: high\nChangelog: Closed model-source 2D Chamfer passes use circular interpolation when the existing sided fit stays within tolerance.\n\nFixes #4411\n",
